{"name":"Lobster Brown","hex":"#a73836","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"lobster","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A crustacean of the Nephropidae family, dark green or blue-black in colour turning bright red when cooked, with a hard shell and claws, which is used as a seafood.","Various other crustaceans that resemble true lobsters:\nA spiny lobster, also called the rock lobster, a crustacean of the Palinuridae family, pinkish red in colour, with a hard, spiny shell but no claws, which is used as a seafood.\nA slipper lobster (a crustacean of the family Scyllaridae).\nA squat lobster."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To fish for lobsters."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lobster"},{"term":"brown","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colour like that of chocolate or coffee.","One of the colour balls used in snooker, with a value of 4 points."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a brown color/colour.","Gloomy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brown"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lob Brown","blocks":[{"text":"William S. \"Lob\" or \"Lobster\" Brown was a college football player."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Lobbrown.jpg/330px-Lobbrown.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lob_Brown","wikidata":"Q18630925"},{"title":"Lobster","blocks":[{"text":"Lobsters are malacostracan decapod crustaceans of the family Nephropidae or its synonym Homaridae. They have long bodies with muscular tails and live in crevices or burrows on the sea floor. Three of their five pairs of legs have claws, including the first pair, which are usually much larger than the others. Highly prized as seafood, lobsters are economically important and are often one of the most profitable commodities in the coastal areas they populate."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Kreeftbij